xpf (0.0.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Add additive structured boundary errors for one prefix site
    (#16133): ControlResponse gains error_code/error_retry_class beside
    the prose error on both Go and Rust sides, and the #10702
    post-teardown refusal (both apply legs) now stamps
    snapshot_post_teardown/retry_debt while keeping the legacy prose
    prefix verbatim, so old binaries classify exactly as before. New Go
    prefers a recognized (code, class) pair but falls back to the prefix
    when the code is empty or unrecognized — no blanket
    unknown=>never-retry rule, and every other prefix site is untouched.
    A wire-level differential matrix (success, false-positive prefix,
    missing fields, prefix-only, code-only, unknown code with/without
