xpf (0.0.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Table-drive the pkg/logging syslog category/severity vocabularies
    (#16179): the four parallel switches (ParseCategory,
    ParseCategoryStrict, ParseSeverity, ParseSeverityStrict) now look up
    explicit tables — one shared categoryVocabulary (the lenient/strict
    category sets are identical; only unknown-name handling differs) and
    two SEPARATE severity tables, keeping the strict SSE vocabulary
    ("" + error/warning/notice/info, case-sensitive) narrower than the
    lenient one (all ten Junos severities, case-insensitive). Sentinel
    rows are explicit: "all"/"" -> 0 for categories, "any"/"" -> 0,
    "none" -> SeverityNone, "emergency" -> SeverityEmergency for
    severities. No behavior change: an exhaustive old-vs-new
    differential test pins every spelling, alias, case variant, and
    invalid token, and the strict parsers keep rejecting every formerly
    rejected name. Config-schema admission vocabulary ownership
    (junosSyslogSeverities in pkg/config/schema_system.go) is unchanged.
    Perf: config/query-time string parsing only, no dataplane hot path;
    the lenient parsers replace a switch with one map lookup.
  * Split the ShowText topic and SystemAction verb metadata (authz price,
    canonical command, fabric admission) into a new metadata-only registry
    package, pkg/optopic (#16136). Typed *Server handlers stay in
    pkg/grpcapi; the registry holds no handler values and depends only on
    pkg/config's permission enum. The grpcapi price tables, cmdtree's
    topic<->command table, authz's verb->command table, and the fabric
    topic allowlist are now derived from the one registry. A new census
    (authz_registry_census_16136_test.go) retains an independent source
    scrape of the handler dispatch and asserts registry == scrape over the
    full topic/verb census, separately for exact/prefix keys, pricing,
    commands, prefix-priced families, and fabric admission. The previously
    unpriced dispatched topic `applications:` is registered at PermView.
    No dispatch change and no new-topic freeze: operator output is
    byte-identical.

